# library/reasoning/corpus/extra/eng-spa.dix -- entries Apertium's eng-spa
# bilingual dictionary lacks, in its own shape, one a line. build.pl reads
# them BEFORE the raw dictionary; an entry both ways is then the first
# meaning of its word in its class, and the first word for its English
# meaning, and an entry marked r="RL" comes after every entry both ways and
# is kept only when the dictionary gave the Spanish word no meaning in that
# class. Every word here has its paradigm in apertium-spa.spa.dix, so the
# builder writes all its forms. A line that is not an entry is a comment.
#
# the Monte Livata article (Italian UD, ISDT test-232..260), into Spanish.
# `niño' and `niña' are what a Spanish article calls a child of four; the
# dictionary's first words for `child', `boy' and `girl' are `infante',
# `chico' and `chica', and `compañero' is what `il compagno della donna' is
# where the dictionary's first word for `partner' is the business `socio'.
<e><p><l>child<s n="n"/></l><r>niño<s n="n"/><s n="GD"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>girl<s n="n"/></l><r>niño<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>boy<s n="n"/></l><r>niño<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>partner<s n="n"/></l><r>compañero<s n="n"/><s n="GD"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>rescuer<s n="n"/></l><r>socorrista<s n="n"/><s n="mf"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>speleological<s n="adj"/></l><r>espeleológico<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>ski<s n="vblex"/></l><r>esquiar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>joke<s n="vblex"/></l><r>bromear<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>patrol<s n="vblex"/></l><r>patrullar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>exhausted<s n="adj"/></l><r>agotado<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>confused<s n="adj"/></l><r>confuso<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>trapped<s n="adj"/></l><r>atrapado<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>extinguish<s n="vblex"/></l><r>apagar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>cleft<s n="n"/></l><r>hendidura<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# the dictionary's first Spanish for `search' is `busca', for `report'
# `denuncia' (to denounce), and it has no `shattered'
<e><p><l>search<s n="n"/></l><r>búsqueda<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>report<s n="vblex"/></l><r>informar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>shattered<s n="adj"/></l><r>destrozado<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>carabineer<s n="n"/></l><r>carabinero<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# `make' is `realizar' first in the dictionary, and `si sono fatti forza',
# `si è fatta male' are made: `hacer'
<e><p><l>make<s n="vblex"/></l><r>hacer<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `mount' is `montura' (a saddle) first: `Monte Livata' is a mountain
<e><p><l>mount<s n="n"/></l><r>monte<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# `know' is `conocer' (to be acquainted with) first; `non si sa come' is
# `no se sabe cómo'
<e><p><l>know<s n="vblex"/></l><r>saber<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `doctor' is the Spanish `doctor' first; a hospital's doctors are `médicos'
<e><p><l>doctor<s n="n"/></l><r>médico<s n="n"/><s n="GD"/></r></p></e>
# `enter' is `introducir' (to put in) and `entrar' has no entry at all:
# `è entrata nel panico' is `ha entrado en pánico'
<e><p><l>enter<s n="vblex"/></l><r>entrar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `arouse' is `excitar' first, which is the wrong sense for a worry:
# `condizioni che non destano preoccupazione'
<e><p><l>arouse<s n="vblex"/></l><r>suscitar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `alejar' has only `move away', more than a word
<e><p><l>distance<s n="vblex"/></l><r>alejar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `operation' is `funcionamiento' first, how a machine runs: `alle
# operazioni di ritrovamento' are the rescue's `operaciones'
<e><p><l>operation<s n="n"/></l><r>operación<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# `hall' is `vestíbulo' first, an entrance: `la sala operativa' is a room
<e><p><l>hall<s n="n"/></l><r>sala<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# `note' is `billete' first, a banknote: `fa sapere, in una nota' is a
# statement the region issued, `una nota'
<e><p><l>note<s n="n"/></l><r>nota<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
#
# the Fiat-Chrysler article, into Spanish. `billion' is `billón' in the
# dictionary, which in Spanish is a million millions -- a thousand times what
# `3,6 miliardi di dollari' says; `millardo' is a thousand millions
<e><p><l>billion<s n="n"/></l><r>millardo<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# `cash' has no Spanish noun: `1,75 miliardi in contanti' is `en efectivo'
<e><p><l>cash<s n="n"/></l><r>efectivo<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# `closing' is `cerramiento' first, an enclosure: a deal's closing is its
# `cierre'; `understanding' is `comprensión' first, and a memorandum of
# understanding is `de entendimiento'; `payable' is `pagable', and a sum
# falling due is `pagadero'
<e><p><l>closing<s n="n"/></l><r>cierre<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>understanding<s n="n"/></l><r>entendimiento<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>payable<s n="adj"/></l><r>pagadero<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
#
# the violin exhibition in Valencia (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-20010202-169), into
# Italian. `rendir', `elogiar', `rasgar' and `instintivo' have their
# paradigms in apertium-spa and no English here: `rendir tributo' renders
# tribute, `elogió su sonoridad' praised it, and a bow scrapes the strings
# (`rasgar' is to tear first, so the entry is read only from Spanish)
<e><p><l>render<s n="vblex"/></l><r>rendir<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>praise<s n="vblex"/></l><r>elogiar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>scrape<s n="vblex"/></l><r>rasgar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>instinctive<s n="adj"/></l><r>instintivo<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
# `medidas coercitivas', where the dictionary puts `coactivo' first
<e><p><l>coercive<s n="adj"/></l><r>coercitivo<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
# `Un capitolo riassume la sperimentazione': the dictionary has no English
# for `resumir', and `summarise' had no Spanish at all
<e><p><l>summarise<s n="vblex"/></l><r>resumir<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `accostarsi con serenità': the dictionary gives `approach' as the
# pronominal `acercarse' only, which the builder does not write
<e><p><l>approach<s n="vblex"/></l><r>acercar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# the Monreale article (Italian UD, VIT-9465..9470), into Spanish: English
# words the Italian side now gives and the Spanish side had no word for,
# and `fiscalía' first for the prosecution where the dictionary's first
# word is the trial's `procesamiento'
<e><p><l>bribe<s n="n"/></l><r>soborno<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>accusation<s n="n"/></l><r>acusación<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>Norman<s n="adj"/></l><r>normando<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>monsignor<s n="n"/></l><r>monseñor<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>prosecutor<s n="n"/></l><r>fiscal<s n="n"/><s n="mf"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>prosecution<s n="n"/></l><r>fiscalía<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>pocket<s n="vblex"/></l><r>embolsar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>swindle<s n="vblex"/></l><r>estafar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>tribunal<s n="n"/></l><r>tribunal<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# the record-market report (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-20010103-139), into Italian:
# `discográfico' and `ralentización' have paradigms in apertium-spa and no
# English here
<e><p><l>discographic<s n="adj"/></l><r>discográfico<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>slowdown<s n="n"/></l><r>ralentización<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# the island-traffic article (Italian UD, VIT-9472..9484), into Spanish:
# `canicular' and `excursionista' have paradigms in apertium-spa and no
# English here
<e><p><l>canicular<s n="adj"/></l><r>canicular<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>excursionist<s n="n"/></l><r>excursionista<s n="n"/><s n="mf"/></r></p></e>
# the opera review (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-20000102-120), into Italian: words
# apertium-spa has a paradigm for and no English here. `convencimiento' is
# a belief, and the English `conviction' is the verdict first in both
# dictionaries, so the IR carries `convincement'; `estreno', `lord' and
# `jalón' are read only into English, so `debut', `lord' and `milestone'
# keep the words they had
<e r="RL"><p><l>debut<s n="n"/></l><r>estreno<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>lord<s n="n"/></l><r>lord<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>convincement<s n="n"/></l><r>convencimiento<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>milestone<s n="n"/></l><r>jalón<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>fatuous<s n="adj"/></l><r>fatuo<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>liceistic<s n="adj"/></l><r>liceístico<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>intone<s n="vblex"/></l><r>entonar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>aria<s n="n"/></l><r>aria<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# the Clinton inquiry (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-19981202-34), all read only into
# English: `la segunda audiencia' -- the dictionary tags the ordinals det ord,
# which the builder does not read, and has `first' and `third' as adjectives
# and `second' not; `está siendo presionado' and `recopilar las últimas
# pruebas' -- the monolingual has both verbs and the bilingual pairs neither
# with an English word
<e r="RL"><p><l>second<s n="adj"/></l><r>segundo<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>pressure<s n="vblex"/></l><r>presionar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
<e r="RL"><p><l>collect<s n="vblex"/></l><r>recopilar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `dicho comité': the committee just named -- apertium-spa has `dicho' as an
# adjective and the bilingual pairs it with nothing, so it read only as the
# participle of `dice' and the phrase had no word before its noun; `la ex
# becaria de la Casa Blanca' is an intern, and the dictionary's `becario'
# is a scholar only
<e><p><l>aforementioned<s n="adj"/></l><r>dicho<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>intern<s n="n"/></l><r>becario<s n="n"/><s n="GD"/></r></p></e>
# the letter on the Bosnian holocaust (Italian UD, VIT-9763..9774): words
# apertium-spa has and the bilingual pairs with nothing -- `bosnio', `víspera'
# -- and two senses first: a petty man is `mezquino', which the bilingual
# did not pair, and to mediate is `mediar', where `intermediar' came first
<e><p><l>bosnian<s n="adj"/></l><r>bosnio<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>eve<s n="n"/></l><r>víspera<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>petty<s n="adj"/></l><r>mezquino<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
<e><p><l>mediate<s n="vblex"/></l><r>mediar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# the pacifist letter, into Spanish
# `dell'"Assalto a Palazzo Farnese"': the assault -- the dictionary's only
# `asalto' is a boxing round
<e><p><l>assault<s n="n"/></l><r>asalto<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# the column on the mobile telephone (AnCora CESS-CAST-P-19990802-48): words
# apertium-spa carries and the bilingual pairs with nothing. `cayó a un
# socavón': a hole in the ground, read only into English so that `hole' is
# still written `hoyo'
<e r="RL"><p><l>hole<s n="n"/></l><r>socavón<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# `el telefonino destripado': gutted
<e><p><l>gut<s n="vblex"/></l><r>destripar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `que yacía junto a él': lay beside him -- English's `lie' is also to tell
# a lie, which Italian writes `mentire', so the pivot is `rest', and read
# only into English so that `rests' is still written `descansa'
<e r="RL"><p><l>rest<s n="vblex"/></l><r>yacer<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `los precios ... se han abaratado': have come down -- read only into
# English, so that `reduces' is still written `reduce'
<e r="RL"><p><l>reduce<s n="vblex"/></l><r>abaratar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `más modernizados': modernised
<e><p><l>modernise<s n="vblex"/></l><r>modernizar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `los publicistas de las marcas': the people who write their advertising
<e><p><l>publicist<s n="n"/></l><r>publicista<s n="n"/><s n="GD"/></r></p></e>
# the letter on the Bastille and Thermidor, into Spanish: words apertium-spa
# carries and the bilingual pairs with nothing. `i presìdi': garrisons
<e><p><l>garrison<s n="n"/></l><r>guarnición<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# `si permette di chiamare fuorilegge': outlaws
<e><p><l>outlaw<s n="n"/></l><r>forajido<s n="n"/><s n="GD"/></r></p></e>
# `la stampa piuttosto tiepida': lukewarm
<e><p><l>lukewarm<s n="adj"/></l><r>tibio<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
# `topi di fogna': sewer rats
<e><p><l>sewer<s n="n"/></l><r>alcantarilla<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# `i lacci e lacciuoli': snares -- written only (r="LR"), so `trampa' is
# still read as a trap
<e r="LR"><p><l>snare<s n="n"/></l><r>trampa<s n="n"/><s n="f"/></r></p></e>
# `non senza redarguire chi ...': rebuke
<e><p><l>rebuke<s n="vblex"/></l><r>reprender<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `il temerario ringhiare di Craxi': the growling -- Spanish says it with the
# noun, `el gruñido'
<e><p><l>growling<s n="n"/></l><r>gruñido<s n="n"/><s n="m"/></r></p></e>
# `perché codesti presìdi non debordino dalle loro funzioni': overstep --
# written only, so `sobrepasa' is still read as `exceeds'
<e r="LR"><p><l>overstep<s n="vblex"/></l><r>sobrepasar<s n="vblex"/></r></p></e>
# `si permette di chiamare fuorilegge': outlaws -- apertium-spa has
# `forajido' as an adjective only, so the noun above has no forms of its own
<e><p><l>outlaw<s n="adj"/></l><r>forajido<s n="adj"/></r></p></e>
